IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `cla-p08-wrongful-death`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 35 and 36 and the Schedule: contracts of minors who have attained 18 years of age, and their legal proceedings.
--
-- A minor "has attained the age of 18 years" on the 18th anniversary of the date of birth (fork F-A2: the anniversary day itself is the
-- first day of being 18).  The helper that finds that anniversary is in cla-p08-wrongful-death.l4 (calendar-month arithmetic, fork F-M1),
-- so a minor born on 29 February attains 18 on 28 February of a year that is not a leap year (fork F-A1; the other reading is 1 March).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Helper -- the age of 18`

-- (not a provision of the Act)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the minor has attained the age of 18 years on` `the date of birth` `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST (`the same day of the month n months later` `the date of birth` 216)

§ `Section 35(1) and (2) -- the effect of a contract by a minor who has attained 18`

-- src:1949 | 35.—(1) Except as otherwise provided by this section or by any
-- src:1950 | other written law, as from 1 March 2009, a contract entered into by a
-- src:1951 | minor who has attained the age of 18 years shall have effect as if he
-- src:1952 | were of full age.
@ref s 35(1) (src:1949-1952)
GIVEN `the date of birth of the minor` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `this section or another written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date on which the contract was entered into` AT LEAST (Date 1 3 2009)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as from 1 March 2009, a contract entered into by a minor who has attained the age of 18 years shall have effect as if he were of full age" -- a date fixed in the text's own words (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a)); see also subsection (6)
        IF NOT (`the minor has attained the age of 18 years on` `the date of birth of the minor` `the date on which the contract was entered into`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a minor who has attained the age of 18 years"
        IF `this section or another written law provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided by this section or by any other written law" -- an exception to a deeming: the deeming does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1956 | (2) Where a minor has, on 1 March 2009, already attained the age of
-- src:1957 | 18 years, subsection (1) shall apply to him and to contracts entered
-- src:1958 | into by him on and after that day.
@ref s 35(2) (src:1956-1958)
GIVEN `the date of birth of the minor` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) subsection (1) applies to the minor and to the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the minor has attained the age of 18 years on` `the date of birth of the minor` (Date 1 3 2009)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a minor has, on 1 March 2009, already attained the age of 18 years, subsection (1) shall apply to him" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)); a minor who attains 18 later is within subsection (1) itself
        IF NOT (`the date on which the contract was entered into` AT LEAST (Date 1 3 2009)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "contracts entered into by him on and after that day" -- a date fixed in the text's own words (rule (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 35(3) to (7) -- what section 35 does not do`

-- src:1962 | (3) Subsection (1) shall not affect or alter —
-- src:1964 | (a) a minor’s lack of capacity to enter into contracts arising
-- src:1965 | from reasons other than because of his age; or
@ref s 35(3)(a) (src:1962-1965)
GIVEN `the lack of capacity arises from reasons other than because of the minor's age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3)(a) subsection (1) affects or alters the minor's lack of capacity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the lack of capacity arises from reasons other than because of the minor's age` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not affect or alter — (a) a minor's lack of capacity to enter into contracts arising from reasons other than because of his age"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a minor's lack of capacity to enter into contracts arising from reasons other than because of his age" -- fork QE: "other than" limits what a flat negative covers, so incapacity because of age gets NOTHING

-- src:1962 | (3) Subsection (1) shall not affect or alter —
-- src:1967 | (b) the application of any provision in any other written law
-- src:1968 | stipulating a requirement as to the attainment of a
-- src:1969 | particular age for the purposes of that written law.
@ref s 35(3)(b) (src:1962-1969)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision in another written law stipulating a requirement as to the attainment of a particular age for the purposes of that written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3)(b) subsection (1) affects the application of the provision of the other written law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is a provision in another written law stipulating a requirement as to the attainment of a particular age for the purposes of that written law` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not affect or alter — ... (b) the application of any provision in any other written law stipulating a requirement as to the attainment of a particular age for the purposes of that written law"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision in any other written law stipulating a requirement as to the attainment of a particular age"

-- src:1973 | (4) The following contracts, if entered into by a minor who has
-- src:1974 | attained the age of 18 years, shall not, by virtue of subsection (1),
-- src:1975 | have effect as if he were of full age:
-- src:1980 | (a) any contract for the sale, purchase, mortgage, assignment
-- src:1981 | or settlement of any land, other than a contract for a lease
-- src:1982 | of land not exceeding 3 years;
-- src:1984 | (b) any contract for a lease of land for more than 3 years;
-- src:1986 | (c) any contract whereby the minor’s beneficial interest under
-- src:1987 | a trust is sold or otherwise transferred to another person, or
-- src:1988 | pledged as a collateral for any purpose;
-- src:1990 | (d) any contract for the settlement of —
-- src:1992 | (i) any legal proceedings or action in respect of which
-- src:1993 | the minor is, pursuant to any written law, considered
-- src:1994 | to be a person under disability on account of his age;
-- src:1995 | or
-- src:1997 | (ii) any claim from which any such legal proceedings or
-- src:1998 | action may arise.
@ref s 35(4) (src:1973-1998)
GIVEN `the minor has attained the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of contract` IS A `Kind of contract by a minor who has attained 18`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(4) the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age by virtue of subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the minor has attained the age of 18 years` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if entered into by a minor who has attained the age of 18 years"
        IF `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract for the sale purchase mortgage assignment or settlement of land` OR `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract for a lease of land for more than 3 years` OR `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract by which the minor's beneficial interest under a trust is sold transferred or pledged` OR `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract for the settlement of legal proceedings in which the minor is under disability on account of age` OR `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract for the settlement of a claim from which such proceedings may arise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following contracts, if entered into by a minor who has attained the age of 18 years, shall not, by virtue of subsection (1), have effect as if he were of full age: (a) any contract for the sale, purchase, mortgage, assignment or settlement of any land ...; (b) any contract for a lease of land for more than 3 years; (c) any contract whereby the minor's beneficial interest under a trust is sold or otherwise transferred ..., or pledged ...; (d) any contract for the settlement of — (i) any legal proceedings or action ...; or (ii) any claim from which any such legal proceedings or action may arise"
        IF `the kind of contract` EQUALS `Contract for a lease of land not exceeding 3 years` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a contract for a lease of land not exceeding 3 years" -- the paragraph takes this lease out of the list, and the subsection says nothing of it (fork QE; the other readings are JUST FALSE and JUST TRUE)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names five kinds and does not say that no other contract is outside subsection (1)

-- src:2002 | (5) Subsection (1) does not entitle —
-- src:2004 | (a) a trustee to pay money or deliver property to a minor who
-- src:2005 | has attained the age of 18 years otherwise than in
-- src:2006 | accordance with the terms of the trust; or
@ref s 35(5)(a) (src:2002-2006)
GIVEN `the payment or delivery is to a minor who has attained the age of 18 years otherwise than in accordance with the terms of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(5)(a) subsection (1) entitles the trustee to pay money or deliver property to the minor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment or delivery is to a minor who has attained the age of 18 years otherwise than in accordance with the terms of the trust` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not entitle — (a) a trustee to pay money or deliver property to a minor who has attained the age of 18 years otherwise than in accordance with the terms of the trust"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in accordance with the terms of the trust"

-- src:2002 | (5) Subsection (1) does not entitle —
-- src:2008 | (b) a minor who has attained the age of 18 years to enter into a
-- src:2009 | contract whereby a trust is extinguished or the terms of a
-- src:2010 | trust are varied, and any such contract entered into by the
-- src:2011 | minor shall not, by virtue of that subsection, have effect as
-- src:2012 | if the minor were of full age.
@ref s 35(5)(b) (src:2002-2012)
GIVEN `the kind of contract` IS A `Kind of contract by a minor who has attained 18`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(5)(b) subsection (1) entitles the minor to enter into the contract and the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of contract`
    WHEN `Contract extinguishing a trust or varying its terms` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not entitle — ... (b) a minor who has attained the age of 18 years to enter into a contract whereby a trust is extinguished or the terms of a trust are varied, and any such contract entered into by the minor shall not, by virtue of that subsection, have effect as if the minor were of full age"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract whereby a trust is extinguished or the terms of a trust are varied"

-- Hand-gathering function (ruling E1, option B as guidance): the effect of the contract, reading (4) and (5)(b) before (1).
-- src:1949 | 35.—(1) Except as otherwise provided by this section or by any
-- src:1950 | other written law, as from 1 March 2009, a contract entered into by a
-- src:1951 | minor who has attained the age of 18 years shall have effect as if he
-- src:1952 | were of full age.
-- src:1973 | (4) The following contracts, if entered into by a minor who has
-- src:1974 | attained the age of 18 years, shall not, by virtue of subsection (1),
-- src:1975 | have effect as if he were of full age:
-- src:2002 | (5) Subsection (1) does not entitle —
@ref s 35 gathered (src:1949-2002)
GIVEN `the date of birth of the minor` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `this section or another written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of contract` IS A `Kind of contract by a minor who has attained 18`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 35(4) the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age by virtue of subsection (1)` (`the minor has attained the age of 18 years on` `the date of birth of the minor` `the date on which the contract was entered into`) `the kind of contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not, by virtue of subsection (1), have effect as if he were of full age" (s 35(4))
        IF `s 35(5)(b) subsection (1) entitles the minor to enter into the contract and the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` `the kind of contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not, by virtue of that subsection, have effect as if the minor were of full age" (s 35(5)(b))
        OTHERWISE `s 35(1) the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` `the date of birth of the minor` `the date on which the contract was entered into` `this section or another written law provides otherwise`

-- src:2016 | (6) Nothing in this section shall apply to or affect any contract that
